<title>UK: TML expresses delight at Eurotunnel ruling.</title>
<headline>TML expresses delight at Eurotunnel ruling.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Channel Tunnel construction firms said on Tuesday that a special arbitration &quot;Panel of Experts&quot; has rejected the bulk of a billion-pound claim for damages by Eurotunnel SA /Plc.</p>
<p>The tunnel operator was seeking damages against the Transmanche Link (TML) consortium of French and British firms in a long-running dispute over the trains they supplied as part of their construction contract.</p>
<p>&quot;The Panel's decision does not recognise any merit in the majority of Eurotunnel's claims and they were rejected on both legal and factual grounds,&quot; TML said in a statement.</p>
</text>
